i5"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257hg-i5"],"id":"long.record-257hg-i5","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 6.121 (Two unconditional safety cases)","locator":"Long record Proposition 6.121, p. 78, label record:257hg-i5","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Under the positive-integer and skipped-step hypotheses of Theorem 6.120, $u=1$ implies $a\\ge1$, so the current remainder is less than $R_k$. Conversely, a fatal tail-mass deficit forces $3a<2u$, hence $u\\ge2$, or $u\\ge3$ when $u$ is odd. These are statements about the current step, not infinite survival.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257hg-i5","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257hg-i5","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i5%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfGreedyFatalGap.three_le_of_fatal_of_odd%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i5%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfGreedyFatalGap.three_le_of_fatal_of_odd%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfGreedyFatalGap.three_le_of_fatal_of_odd"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257hg-i5","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i5%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfGreedyFatalGap.two_le_of_fatal%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i5